    {
      "id": "docs-agent-trading",
      "scenario": "docs",
      "surface": "docs",
      "args": {
        "files": [
          "docs/agent-trading.md",
          "apps/docs/src/content/docs/developers/agent-trading.md",
          "apps/frontend/public/docs/agent-trading.md"
        ]
      },
      "outcome": {
        "text": "#### Which perps count for an agent: by order, not by wallet\n\nAn agent's perps record holds the fills of the Hyperliquid orders its own keys built through\nCandle, matched by client order id (`cloid`): opens, closes, Candle modifies (the replacement\norder carries its own cloid) and take-profit / stop-loss legs (a triggered leg keeps its cloid).\nOn an EVM TEE wallet every fill is the bound key's, as before; where a key's order rests across a\nrebind and fills after it, the order's key wins over the binding period.\n\nPerps traded from the owner's **embedded wallet** (`walletId: \"embedded\"`) count the same way.\nOne embedded wallet can carry the owner's own trades and several agents' orders, so the record\nnever credits the wallet as a whole: a fill no Candle order of an agent key claims (the owner's\nown trade, another tool, an order modified outside Candle) is in no public figure, rank, round,\nchart or position. No fill counts for two agents. Each agent keeps its own position in a coin it\nshares with the owner or another agent: its own size and average entry, its unrealized P&L at the\nvenue's mark, and its share of each hour's funding by its share of the size. A liquidation,\nauto-deleveraging or settlement (no Candle order) is shared among the holders of the position by\ntheir sizes. Where a split cannot be exact (holders on opposite sides of a coin, a forced fill\nshared, an unmatched fill while the agent is in the coin, funding whose size disagrees, a gap in\nthe venue's fill history), the round carries `partial: true` and `partialReasons`, and the window\nis `perpsPartial`. An embedded wallet's round has `hash: null` and its position rows have\n`liquidationPx` and `liquidationDistance` `null` unless the agent holds the whole position: no\npublic answer names the embedded wallet or shows the owner's own trades. Those trades show only\nin the owner's console.\n\n`series` contains the newest 2,000 realized points, oldest first, and `seriesTruncated` says\nwhether older points were omitted. `scannedTrades` and `truncated` describe the stored\nrefresh's coverage. Before the first refresh, a newly published profile returns an empty record."
      }
    }
  ]
